. Basic Commands

ls : to list the directory and files
cd : to redirect to any folder/directory
pwd : to check the present working directory
mkdir : to create a new directory
rm : to remove/delete the files
rmdir : to remove the folder/directory
cat, zcat : to view the files
touch : to create a new files
head : to view the top lines of the files
tail, tail -f : to view the bottom lines of the files
less, more : to view thww files in a pagenated way
cp, cp -r : to copy the files and folders
mv : to move the files and also to rename the files and directories
wc : to count the words from the files
vi, vim : to edit the files
ln (Hardlink & Softlink) : to create the shortcut of the files
cut : to cut the context or specific text from the files
tee : to print and insert the file
sort : to sort the files in alphabatically
clear : to clear the screen or terminal
diff : to check the difference between the files
ssh : to connect the remote VM or Instance with local system
df : to check the storage and disk of the system
du : to check the storage and folders
ps : to check the bash and id
top : to check the all running processes in the system
fuser : to check the file system process
kill : to kill any of the process
nohup : to store the output in file
free : to check the RAM and storage
vmstat : to check the RAM and Stats


. System Level Commands

uname : to check which platform is in current use
uptime : to check the uptime of the system
date : to check the current date of the system
who, whoami : to check which user is logged in when/ and check the current user
which : to check the version and location
id : to check the GID and user
sudo (Super User Do) : to get the access and permission
shutdown : to shutdown the system
reboot : to reboot the system
apt : to update and install the new packages on the system


. User & Group Management Commands

sudo (Super User Do) : to get the access and permission
useradd -m : to add the new user in the home
whoami : to check the current user
su : to switch the users
passwd : to set the password of the users
userdel : to delete the users
groupadd : to create new groups for the users
gpasswd -a, -m : to add users into the groups
groupdel : to delete the groups


. File Permission Commands

umask : to check the by default permissions
ls -l : to check the permissions of the files and folders
chmod : to change the permissions of the files
chown : to change the ownership of the files
chgrp : to change the ownership of the groups


. Compression Commands

zip, gunzip, gzip : to compress the files
tar, untar : to compress the files


. File Transfer Commands

scp : to copy the files and folders from local to remote
rsync : to sync the files and folders between local and remote


