ping : to check the connectivity and reachability of the website or ip
nestat : to check the internet connection and network
ifconfig : to check the IP & network interface
traceroute, tracepath : to trace the routes of the website
mtr : to check the path and ping
nslookup : to check the domain and ip
telnet : to check the domain and port no
hostname : to check the hostname of the system
IP : to check the IP of the system
iwconfig : to check the wireless connection
ss : to check the internet connection and networks
arp : to find the MAC address of the system
dig : to check where is the website is hosted
whois : to check the full details with proper info
route : to check the routes
nmap : to scan the websites
wget : to download the files from the web
watch : to check the status for every 2 sec
curl : to call the API endpoint
jq : to sort the API's


. Curl vs Wget

wget : used to get the data from the Web
curl : used to get the data from the Web & API testing


. Process Management 

ps: to check the process
ps -e : to check the processes in detail
ps aux : to check the processes in more detail
ps -ef : to check the process parent and child


. AWK , SED , GREP

grep 'pattern' file name : to find the words and lines
grep -i 'pattern' file name : to find the incentative cases
grep -v 'pattern' file name : to reverse the condition
grep -n 'pattern' file name : to find the lines and lines no
grep -c 'pattern' file name : to print the matching lines
grep -E 'pattern' file name : to extend and print or the values
grep -r 'pattern' file name : to find the values recursively
grep -w 'pattern' file name : to find the exact match
grep 'A' 'pattern' file name : to find the values from the specific

sed 'p' file name : to print the lines
sed -n '3p' file name : to print the specific lines
sed -n '4p,5p' file name : to print the multiple lines
sed 'xyz /d' file name : to delete the lines which mentioned
sed '/d' file name : to delete the specific lines
sed 'li\ xyz xyz' file name : to add a new line in the file
sed '3a\ xyz xyz' file name : to append the new line



